  <article class="prose plain">
    <h1>About this archive</h1>

    <p>
      This site is a rebuilt archive of a full undergraduate course in system
      analysis and design. The source material is a set of lecture decks; the
      writing here is not a transcript of them. Each lecture has been rewritten
      as a standalone lesson that assumes no prior knowledge and fills in the
      background the slides took for granted.
    </p>

    <h2>What was kept and what was dropped</h2>
    <p>
      The lessons keep the course's structure and its diagrams. Everything tied
      to sitting the exam — past papers, mark schemes, model answers, revision
      checklists — has been removed. This is meant to be read to understand the
      subject, not to pass a test on it.
    </p>

    <h2>Diagrams</h2>
    <p>
      No diagram on this site is redrawn. Every figure is a screenshot of the
      original lecture slide it came from, and its caption names the deck and
      slide number.
    </p>

    <h2>Credits</h2>
    <p>
      Compiled and rewritten by
      <a href="https://syedmehedihussain.com">Syed Mehedi Hussain</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Based on the System Analysis and Design course, Department of Computer
      Science and Engineering, Independent University, Bangladesh — taught by
      Dr. Razib Hayat Khan. The lecture slides are the source of every diagram
      and of the course's structure; the explanatory text is new.
    </p>

    <h2>Source</h2>
    <p>
      The site is built with Astro and deploys from
      <a href="https://github.com/syedmehedihussain/system-design">its repository</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Page>
